 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S5981",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5981-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5981\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law,\nin relation to a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on\ncertain premises\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis legislation would create an exemption for the Lewiston Fire\nCompany Number 1 as it pertains to the 200 foot rule for on premise\nconsumption of alcohol.  SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: Section 1\nallows the authority to issue a retail license for on-premise\nconsumption for the Lewiston fire department which is located within\n200 feet of a church. This section contains the appropriate\ndesignation of property for this siting.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Lewiston Fire Company No.1 recently completed renovations to their\nfacility including the creation of a small reception hall to be used\nfor weddings and other events.Due to the proximity to St. Peters\nChurch and School they are prohibited from being issued a license for\non-premise consumption from the State Liquor Authority. St. Peters\nChurch and School supports the Lewiston Fire Company No. 1's attempt\nto secure a license. This legislation like many before it simply seeks\nto create an exemption to the 200 foot rule so that the Fire Company\nmay apply for a license.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
